KZ2 patch 6095 (fps-why 2026-11-24 R5): one cold "diagnostics armed" flag in ps3_indirect_call.
ps3_indirect_call_entry and ps3_indirect_call_impl_at (patch 6094) tested about fifteen getenv-cached switches on every
indirect call: PPU_CSCHECK, PS3_ICALL_GATE, BCTRL_RING, PS3_BREADCRUMB, PPU_TOCWATCH, PS3_CALLTRACE(_LR/_TO/_FROM/_R5),
FLOW_FORCE_RTCFG, SPURS_TRACE, PS3_PRX_CALLTRACE, PPU_TOCFIX, PPU_RETWATCH (indirect-call diagnostics were 4.1 % of
ppu-main's samples). s_icall_diag, decided once at the first indirect call, is 1 when any of them is set; when it is
0 the impl skips every diagnostic block, which with its switch unset did nothing. When one is set every block runs as
before and tests its own switch. Bit-exact by construction; the host test checks that the list names every getenv of
the two functions outside the cold addr == 0 path (PS3_NULL_CALL, PPU_OPD_RECOVER stay where they are).
ASSUMPTION (as patch 7003): nothing sets these variables after the first indirect call (main applies kz2.ini first).
Expected (ASSUMPTION, fps-why): 0.5-1 ms of ppu-main per heavy frame; judged on the ps3_indirect_call_impl share.
Host test: tools/runtime/test_ppu_icall_diag.sh (with negative controls).

